Your task\
\
Use the existing bootstrap scaffold to prepare this repository for production-quality AI-assisted development.\
\
Do the following:\
\
1. Audit the repository\
\
Inspect the current repo structure, existing files, package setup, documentation, tests, CI/CD, hooks, branches, and git status.\
\
Create or update:\
\
- BOOTSTRAP_AUDIT.md\
- STALE_ITEMS.md\
- CURRENT_STATE.md\
- AI_HANDOFF.md\
\
Clearly separate:\
\
- existing useful files\
- stale or conflicting files\
- missing files\
- assumptions\
- open questions\
- risks\
\
Do not overwrite valuable existing files without preserving useful content.\
\
2. Extract requirements\
\
From the project input, extract:\
\
- product goals\
- target users\
- core workflows\
- functional requirements\
- non-functional requirements\
- integrations\
- data needs\
- security/privacy concerns\
- observability needs\
- assumptions\
- open questions\
\
Create or update:\
\
- PROJECT_MEMORY.md\
- OPEN_QUESTIONS.md\
\
Do not invent missing requirements. If something is unclear but not blocking, document a safe assumption. If it is blocking, document it as an open question.\
\
3. Create the initial specs\
\
Create project-specific specs under:\
\
- SPECS/\
