\
- system overview\
- main components\
- data model direction\
- API boundaries\
- integration points\
- deployment assumptions\
- security/privacy considerations\
- observability needs\
- failure modes\
- risks\
- implementation phases\
\
Create ADRs for meaningful decisions such as framework choice, persistence model, API style, deployment model, auth model, or major architectural boundaries.\
\
5. Create the backlog\
\
Create or update:\
\
- BACKLOG.md\
- BACKLOG/BACKLOG_INDEX.md\
- BACKLOG/<backlog-item>.md where useful\
\
The backlog must be sequenced by dependency and implementation order, not just feature order.\
\
Each backlog item must include:\
\
- title\
- purpose\
- scope\
- linked spec\
- linked acceptance criteria\
- dependencies\
- risks\
- priority\
- complexity\
- readiness status\
- suggested owner role\
- test expectations\
- definition of done\
- whether it can run in parallel\
- file ownership boundaries if parallel work is safe\
