\
- phases\
- task order\
- dependencies\
- first safe implementation task\
- recommended first branch\
- test approach\
- review approach\
- release/readiness approach\
\
The parallel execution plan must clearly say which tasks can run in parallel and which must stay sequential.\
\
Do not allow parallel work if tasks touch shared architecture, shared schemas, shared APIs, dependencies, CI/CD, auth, deployment, or global configuration without coordination.\
